{{> adminTop}}<div class="notice info">The four canonical learning areas keep historical assessments comparable. Courses and individual questions map to these areas; career pathways select their required areas. Descriptions can be maintained here without renaming historical results.</div><form class="card" method="post" action="/admin/competencies"><input type="hidden" name="_csrf" value="{{csrf}}">{{#each domains}}<label class="field">{{name}}<textarea name="domain{{index}}" rows="3" maxlength="1000" placeholder="Define expected knowledge, practical evidence and limits of assessment.">{{description}}</textarea></label>{{/each}}<button class="button">Save competency definitions</button></form><section class="card space-top"><h2>Current evidence policy</h2><ul class="workflow-list"><li>Use the latest completed attempt once per course; retakes do not stack the matching score.</li><li>Use latest diagnostic evidence where no completed course exists in an area.</li><li>75% identifies a knowledge gap; strong alignment requires all career areas assessed, no area below 75%, and an average of at least 85%.</li><li>When completed practical evidence exists, alignment uses 70% knowledge and 30% faculty rubric evidence. Practical rubrics also gate required course completion. Self-declared qualifications and ongoing courses are not earned competency.</li></ul><a class="text-link" href="/admin/careers">Manage career pathway requirements →</a></section>{{> adminBottom}}
